WEBVTT

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.000
Today, Satoshi and his Pokémon...

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.130
...once again continue their training
for the Masters Tournament.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.880
Looking good, everyone!
You’ve got it!

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.880
Looks like
it’s all coming together.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.380
Still more to go!

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.100
I’ve gotta help them
get a lot faster and even more powerful!

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.260
I see.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.140
But what specifically
do you plan to do?

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.430
I’m gonna get all fired up,
and so are they!

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.100
Huh?

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.520
But... how exactly?

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.150
Huh?

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.060
Like I said, we’ll get fired up...

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.150
Incoming call from the Professor.
Incoming call from the Professor.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.320
Hello.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.900
Hey, Satoshi!

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.160
Professor Okido!

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.200
You should come by sometime.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.410
All of your Pokémon are—

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.410
That’s it!

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.500
I know where we can go
to get fired up!

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.170
Okido Laboratory, Kanto Region

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.960
Go! I heard from Shigeru.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.670
You managed to get into Project Mew?
Congratulations!

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.050
That’s right, thank you!

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.170
We better keep up!

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.470
Oh, Bayleaf!

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.650
You been doing good?

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.290
Thanks for the grand welcome!

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.790
All right!
Come on out, everyone!

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.360
Everyone,
I’ve got something to announce!

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:39.200
There’s this huge tournament coming up
called the Masters Tournament,

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.830
and we’re gonna battle in it.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.910
We’re gonna win, win, win,

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.960
and win our way
to battling the Champion, Mr. Dande!

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.170
So I want you guys to
share your power with us!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.820
Amazing!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.030
Such passionate cheers!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.490
I took in your power,
you guys!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.260
Gänger!

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.200
Gänger!

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.080
Elecible!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.550
That was your Gänger?

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:17.670
Shinji!

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.760
Huh? What?

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.890
You okay?

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:27.930
It’s hot!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.640
Huh? How come?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.020
Gänger’s always cold to the touch...

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.610
Huh? It <i>is</i> cold...

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.360
Huh?

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.200
H-Huh? You’re right...

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.330
You’re hopeless.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.990
At least <i>try</i> to understand
your partner’s condition.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.160
I <i>do</i> understand!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.420
Satoshi, do you know him?

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:57.630
Yeah, he’s a rival I battled again and again,
back when I was on my journey around Sinnoh.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.840
His name’s Shinji.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.090
Nice to meet you...
My name’s Go.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.510
Is it just me,
or is he kinda scary?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.350
He’s always like this.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.020
Satoshi! Go!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.440
Professor Okido!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.570
Professor!
Shinji’s here!

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.320
You see,
I thought to surprise you.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:23.950
Huh?

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:28.200
Shinji happened to turn up yesterday,
just out of the blue.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.210
Professor Okido is the leading authority
on Pokémon research.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.130
Anyone wanting to learn all they can
about Pokémon would visit him.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.750
There’s nothing strange about it.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.260
You gonna train together?

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:48.970
We should, too...

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.930
Leave it to your Pokémon.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.310
That’s what this place is for.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.230
I’ll go watch over them!

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.230
Satoshi, you must have plenty
to catch up on with Shinji!

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.070
Yeah!

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.320
Goukazaru, you go with them.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.620
Take care of Gänger,
Goukazaru.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.790
Goukazaru listens to
Shinji’s orders, too...?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.840
Yeah, he used to be
Shinji’s Pokémon.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.340
What?!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.050
Shinji, a trainer that Satoshi met
in the Sinnoh Region.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.510
He put his Hikozaru through harsh training
time and time again,

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.060
but eventually
abandoned him as a failure.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.180
Satoshi befriended
that same Hikozaru,

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:40.020
cared deeply for him,
and led him to evolve into a Goukazaru.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.070
What a history...

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.030
Yeah.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.700
Goukazaru’s sure gotten stronger.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.710
Hey, Sarunori!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.470
Elecible, go play with them.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.520
Gamagaru and Fukamaru
really like cuddling up to you.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:57.100
Ooh! Are the Fire-type Pokémon
teaching Gänger a new move?

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.850
Quite a novel discovery!

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.440
You didn’t participate
in the Championships, Shinji?

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:44.230
I’m not one for festivities.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.690
Then why don’t we
take advantage of the moment?

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.650
Battle me!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.860
Oh, there he goes!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.620
3v3 with no switching.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:56.740
Okay!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.200
But...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:02.080
Only use Pokémon you’re using
in the Masters Tournament.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.630
Okay!
I’ll call everyone over!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.520
Good, good.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.270
Hey! Gänger!

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.910
Thanks, Goukazaru!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.630
Gänger, that was
Will-O-Wisp, wasn’t it?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.760
Satoshi...

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.800
He accomplished it thanks to
Goukazaru and the others’ advice.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.760
They are truly
dependable mentors.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.050
I see.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.810
Thanks, Goukazaru.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:01.680
And thank you, everyone!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.790
Let’s go, Shinji!

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.000
Lucario! I choose you!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.000
Stand by for battle!

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:39.850
Gyarados...

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:55.530
Lucario! Shadow Clones!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.910
Ice Fang!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:06.920
Not even close!

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:08.370
Destroyer Beam!

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.100
Now’s your chance!

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.850
He won’t be able to move for a while
after Destroyer Beam.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.350
This is Satoshi’s chance.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.560
Aura Sphere!

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.650
Charge in!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.820
Lucario!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.490
Ice Fang!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.830
Lucario!

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.600
What’s that?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.610
Lucario, is that...?

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.490
That’s it... Come on!

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.320
Destroyer Beam!

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:28.250
Now! Bullet Punch!

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:51.230
All right!

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.240
You did well.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.280
Thank you.
Your Bullet Punch was awesome.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.990
Professor, what was that?

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:11.620
Its Steel-type energy blazed up
from being backed into a corner,

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.290
and let it activate Bullet Punch.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:18.300
Next up, Kairyu!
I choose you!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.390
Stand by for battle,
Gaburias!

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.770
Gaburias next, huh?

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.270
Dragon Claw!

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:37.360
We’ll use Dragon Claw, too!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.200
Equally matched...

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:48.950
Are you sure?

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.330
Stone Edge!

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.080
Hurricane!

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:05.720
Such incredible power...

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:07.100
Draco Meteor!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.110
We’ll use Draco Meteor, too!

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.200
Kairyu!
Charge in with the Draco Meteor!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.540
Here come his crazy tactics!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.510
Dragon Claw!

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.190
Kairyu!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.570
He lost...

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:06.950
Nevertheless, that Draco Meteor
was quite an interesting strategy.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.740
Kairyu, you were
really cool out there.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.120
Take a rest!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.830
Did you see that, Shinji?
I call that Dra-Kairyu Meteor!

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:20.840
How tacky.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:25.880
It’s cool!
‘Cause I think it’s cool!

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.800
Stand by for battle,
Metagross!

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.180
Metagross, huh?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.560
Huh? Shinji’s Pokémon...

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:42.690
Gyarados, Gaburias, Metagross...

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:46.650
This time...
Gänger, I choose you!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.790
They’re really excited.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.420
They’re about to see
the results of their training.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:04.880
Gänger! Goukazaru and the others
are watching! Give it your all!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.300
Agility!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:16.520
Shadow Ball!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.480
Psychokinesis!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.370
Gänger!

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.450
You call yourself
one of the Masters Eight?!

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:48.010
If you’re struggling against <i>me,</i>
then you’ll have no hope of winning.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:49.220
Comet Punch!

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.520
Can you keep going, Gänger?

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.280
That’s right, Gänger!
We have everyone from the lab on our side!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.200
Let’s show it to Shinji!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:16.990
Will-O-Wisp!

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:23.790
Ooh, it’s started!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.880
I get it! It felt hot before
because it was awakening a new move!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.470
Do it!

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.360
All right! It worked!

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.780
Comet Punch!

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.500
Is the burn affecting us?

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.750
Now! Shadow Ball!

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:21.060
We did it!

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.770
All right, Satoshi won!

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.030
You did it, Gänger!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.040
Goukazaru, Lizardon, all you guys...
Thank you!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.420
You did well.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:49.750
Um...

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:54.880
Your three Pokémon were all aces
of the Masters Eight, weren’t they?

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.680
Gyarados is Mr. Wataru’s...

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.680
Gaburias is Ms. Shirona’s...

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.930
Metagross is Mr. Daigo’s...

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.930
Was that really a coincidence?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.150
Professor,
thank you for everything.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.440
With that, I’ll be off.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.690
You can come back whenever.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.570
Right. Then excuse me.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.570
See you again, Goukazaru.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:21.990
Let’s go, Elecible.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:27.250
Shinji!
Let’s battle again sometime!

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.590
He’s way too cool, yeah.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:37.800
Apparently, Shinji has been asked
to become a Gym Leader.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.220
A Gym Leader?!

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:43.720
And that is the reason
he wanted to learn more about Pokémon.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:47.190
Professor...
I’m glad I came back.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:49.650
Thanks to everyone,
I’m all fired up now!

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.320
I’m gonna go all the way
and even beat Mr. Dande!

00:20:57.070 --> 00:21:00.530
Go! Let’s head to
the Masters Tournament right now!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.450
Yeah!

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.790
Satoshi!

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.960
Mom!
When’d you get here?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.790
Partway through your battle.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.630
Huh? You saw it?!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.170
You must be tired
from all your battling.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.170
You should sleep at home tonight.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.010
You’re welcome too, Go. Okay?

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:22.800
I-Is that okay, Satoshi?
For me to intrude...

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.470
It’s fine, it’s fine!

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:25.890
Thanks, Mom.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.310
His traveling companions
he hadn’t seen in a while...

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:37.110
...and his battle with his rival Shinji
have stoked the fire in Satoshi and company even more.

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:41.990
Next time, the curtain finally rises
on the Masters Tournament!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:15.500
The Masters Tournament
is finally starting!

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:18.380
I’m standing among
all these amazing members...

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:21.420
Next stop:
Our battle with Mr. Dande!

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:23.800
Pikachu, let’s go all out!

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:26.430
Go for it, Satoshi!

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:27.510
I’ll be cheering for you!

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:29.100
Yeah!

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:31.350
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.190
The Curtain Rises!
The Masters Tournament!!
